# Meridian — Cloudflare response headers (F1: immutable caching)
# Deployed location: root of the static output (dist/client/_headers),
# copied there by the build from public/_headers. Honoured by Cloudflare
# Pages and Workers Static Assets, which serve the live site; GitHub Pages
# ignores this file (harmless).
#
# Scope: ONLY /assets/* — the Vite/Rolldown build output. Every file there
# is content-hashed (a content change produces a new filename/URL), so a
# cached copy can never go stale and is safe to cache for a year as
# immutable. This matches the rule the Nitro/Vercel build already emits
# in .vercel/output/config.json for /assets/(.*).
#
# Deliberately NOT immutable: everything else keeps Cloudflare's default
# (public, max-age=0, must-revalidate). /flags.json, /audio/*, /icons/*,
# /images/*, /loop/*, sw.js and HTML all have stable names with mutable
# content (e.g. narration mp3s were replaced under the same filenames in
# PR #174, and sw.js is re-fingerprinted every build), so they must keep
# revalidating — no rule below touches them.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
